base-mismatch: err=refused: phantom-merge guard: PR #3 is based on "main", not the feature branch "feature/4a17-version" — merging it would land work where nobody is looking (D5) |   why:  the forge understood the call and declined it — a domain refusal, not a transient fault |   do:   fix the request so it satisfies the refusal; resending it unchanged will fail again
no-review: err=refused: forge.merge gate: PR #4 has no review at all — nothing has been APPROVED — the merge is refused BEFORE the forge is asked (L34/D10) |   why:  the forge understood the call and declined it — a domain refusal, not a transient fault |   do:   fix the request so it satisfies the refusal; resending it unchanged will fail again
approved: pr=4 alreadyMerged=false evidenceKeys=checks,review_at,review_by,review_state,threads
approved: mergeSHA-shape=$SHA
phantom: type=*PhantomMergeError err=phantom merge (D5): PR #5 reported merged at $SHA but that commit is not an ancestor of feature/4a17-version — the work is NOT where the loop believes it is; verify the squash SHA (the task branch's originals are never ancestors after a squash — checking them would call every correct merge a failure)
